# SQL scripts

- Read `sql/AI-INSTRUCTIONS.md` and platform-specific instructions (`azure-sql-db`, `sql-server-mi`, `common`).
- Scripts are for DBA review — never auto-run destructive DDL/DML against live systems.
- Prefer additive scripts; document rollback and permission requirements in comments or companion docs.
- Do not hard-code production credentials, server names, or environment-specific retention.
- Keep Azure SQL DB and SQL Server MI scripts separated by capability differences.
- Update usage-tracking / audit docs when new telemetry or audit objects are introduced.
